  "title": "BCI Report: public EEG decoding results reported with their protocol",
  "creators": [
    {
      "name": "BCI Report"
    }
  ],
  "description": "<p>Cohort-level EEG decoding results, each published with the protocol that produced it: cohort, electrode count, evaluation split, chance level, interval and known limitations. No raw EEG, no per-participant scores, no model weights and no overall ranking.</p><p>The site, with every figure in context: <a href=\"https://bci.report/\">https://bci.report/</a>. The release log, with the SHA-256 of every file: <a href=\"https://bci.report/releases/\">https://bci.report/releases/</a>.</p><p>Cite BCI Report and the release you used (this archive’s version is the release id), and the upstream dataset each figure was computed on: every dataset page gives its credit, <a href=\"https://bci.report/datasets/\">https://bci.report/datasets/</a>.</p>",
  "access_right": "open",
  "license": "cc-by-4.0",
  "notes": "The aggregate results in this archive are CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-DATA): measurements this project produced. The code is under the MIT License (LICENSE). The EEG recordings the results were computed from are not included and keep their own licences and terms.",
